1
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:04,978
Welcome to the Watermill Inn.

2
00:00:04,978 --> 00:00:05,956
Oh, Richard,

3
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:08,934
it's exactly as it was when we were married!

4
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:10,961
And when I got married.

5
00:00:10,961 --> 00:00:14,452
Even the old patchwork quilt is the same!

6
00:00:14,452 --> 00:00:16,740
My great-grandmother made that quilt

7
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,588
when Teddy Roosevelt was President.

8
00:00:18,588 --> 00:00:21,466
In those days, when they made quilts.

9
00:00:21,466 --> 00:00:25,824
they cut patches

10
00:00:25,824 --> 00:00:28,722
so that each one would be a part of it.

11
00:00:28,722 --> 00:00:29,780
What a lovely tradition!

12
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:31,780
Thank you for calling us.

13
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:35,736
I remember you and your wife

14
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:37,736
We were very young.

15
00:00:37,736 --> 00:00:40,434
And very much in love.

16
00:00:40,434 --> 00:00:41,692
We have a baby now.

17
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:45,565
How wonderful! A boy or a girl?

18
00:00:45,565 --> 00:00:47,647
A boy--Max.

19
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:49,647
Do you have a picture?

20
00:00:49,647 --> 00:00:53,603
Would a professional photographer be without a picture?

21
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:57,749
Oh, he's adorable!

22
00:00:57,749 --> 00:00:59,559
And very bright.

23
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:02,062
Like his father. A real Stewart.

24
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:04,239
And very good-looking, like his mother.

25
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:06,955
Well, it's nice to have you with us again.

26
00:01:06,955 --> 00:01:08,493
Next time, bring the baby.

27
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:11,471
You see, Richard? Max is welcome here.

28
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:12,787
Not on our anniversary.

29
00:01:12,787 --> 00:01:15,798
This vacation is for you and me.

30
00:01:15,798 --> 00:01:18,180
If there's anything you need, please call me.

31
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:20,405
I'll be in the front office all day.

32
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:29,339
Oh, I took the liberty of ordering some breakfast for you.

33
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:50,185
Just put it over there, Charles.

34
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:53,163
Thank you, Charles.

35
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:56,140
Compliments of the Watermill Inn.

36
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:57,140
Thank you.

37
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:59,118
Thank you so much.

38
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:08,052
Now, this is my idea of a good time.

39
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:14,608
Let's see ... hotcakes and maple syrup, with scrambled eggs.

40
00:02:14,608 --> 00:02:18,486
Umm ... smell that coffee ... cinnamon and cloves.

41
00:02:18,486 --> 00:02:19,611
Homemade buttermilk biscuits.

42
00:02:19,611 --> 00:02:22,942
Slices of orange with burnt honey.

43
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:23,591
Let's eat!

44
00:02:23,591 --> 00:02:25,538
First I want to call home

45
00:02:25,538 --> 00:02:27,740
and check on your mother and the baby.

46
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:28,625
Honey, if there were any problems,

47
00:02:28,625 --> 00:02:29,871
she would call us.

48
00:02:29,871 --> 00:02:31,876
She doesn't know we've changed hotels.

49
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:40,810
You're right. Of course.

50
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:43,788
Hello, operator.

51
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:55,700
I'd like to call Riverdale, New York.

52
00:02:55,700 --> 00:03:04,884
This food is heavenly, isn't it?

53
00:03:04,884 --> 00:03:06,134
This whole place is heavenly.

54
00:03:06,134 --> 00:03:10,589
Do you remember that old desk?

55
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:12,732
Mrs. Montefiore told me that

56
00:03:12,732 --> 00:03:14,703
George Washington sat at that desk

57
00:03:14,703 --> 00:03:16,545
and wrote to his wife Martha.

58
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:19,523
What do you want to do after breakfast?

59
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:22,501
Why don't we take a walk down to the river?

60
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:24,181
In the rain?

61
00:03:24,181 --> 00:03:31,435
No. Look out the window. The sun is shining!

62
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:34,435
Now this is my idea of a good time!
